  "faithful": "ERIGERON, or SWEET FLEA BANE, in botany, a genus of the syngenesia polygamia superflua clasfs. The receptacle is naked; the pappus is hairy; and the radii of the corolla are linear and very narrow. There are fifteen species, two of which are natives of Britain, viz. the acre, or blue-flowered flea-bane; and the canadense, or Canada flea-bane.",
